Documentation for merge_h7dev_to_h8dev.sh
-----------------------------------------


# For use on HeuristRef.net only
# Merges changes in h7dev into a development branch h8dev
# Fails and emails server managers if there are merge conflicts (successful merge does not mean the code is coherent ...)
# ChatGPT 21 april 2026

Use it with cron like this:

MAILTO=support@heuristnetwork.org

15 2 * * * /usr/local/bin/nightly_merge_h7_to_h8.sh > /dev/null

Notes for your developers:

this should run in a separate clone, not in a working copy anyone edits manually
it will push automatically only if the merge succeeds
if the merge fails, it prints the conflict details to stderr, exits non-zero, and cron will email the error output to MAILTO
origin/h8dev is left untouched on failure

One small practical point: if the server may create merge commits without a configured git identity, set these once in that clone or for that user:

git config user.name "Heurist nightly merge"
git config user.email "support@heuristnetwork.org"
